    "cols2_copy_387976406": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "courtney.dickens@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "courtney.dickens@stryker.com",
      "jcr:created": "Fri Jun 06 2025 21:03:22 GMT+0000",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Fri Jun 06 2025 21:03:22 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/columncontrol/cols2",
      "col1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "text": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "courtney.dickens@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "courtney.dickens@stryker.com",
          "jcr:created": "Fri Jun 06 2025 21:04:00 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<p>This cutting and drilling guide for maxillofacial surgeons is a combination of a nylon occlusal guide and titanium cutting/drilling guide, the latest enhancement to 3D Systems’ VSP surgical planning solutions portfolio.</p>\n<p><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\">Features and benefits:</span></span></p>\n<p><b>Easy guide placement</b><br>\nOcclusal-based registration enabled by an easy-to-use connection site with indicators to confirm the proper connection of guides.</p>\n<p><b>Reduced bulkiness</b><br>\nLower profile guides are easier to place in areas with limited exposure.</p>\n<p><b>Multi-material benefits</b><br>\nOcclusal registration from a nylon guide for accurate placement plus the increased strength and rigidity<sup>2</sup> of a titanium cutting/drilling guide.<br>\n</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Jun 10 2025 14:04:16 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      },
